# `call (%r2), zero, (%r1)` writes %r2, so the address through it is not
# the thread index's but `addr ?`, a value `call` defines; it was read as
# `4 * %tid.x + param_0` with the call unparsed, where ptxas stores to
# param_0. A `.param` return value is one per thread (PTX ISA §5.1.6,
# Table 7): the address through it depends on a value loaded from
# memory; it was read as a uniform value, `[uniform(%rd2@68) + param_0]`,
# 1 sector, where thread t stores at param_0 + 4t.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/call_returns.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_call_returns( // block 32×1×1 | per CTA: global store 128 B; param load 256 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (value defined by unsupported instruction `call`){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_call_param_returns( // block 32×1×1 | per CTA: global store 128 B; param load 512 B, store 128 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (depends on a value loaded from memory){{$}}
